### POST /v1/responses

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/ai-gateway/security-and-compliance/zdr

Enforce Zero Data Retention for the Vercel AI Gateway Responses API. This endpoint allows for structured input and routing through ZDR-compliant providers.

```APIDOC
## POST /v1/responses

### Description
Enforce Zero Data Retention for the Responses API.

### Method
POST

### Endpoint
/v1/responses

### Parameters
#### Request Body
- **model** (string) - Required - The model to use.
- **input** (array) - Required - List of input objects (e.g., messages).
- **providerOptions** (object) - Optional - Configuration for the AI Gateway.
  - **gateway** (object) - Optional
    - **zeroDataRetention** (boolean) - Optional - Set to true to route the request only through providers that have zero data retention agreements.

### Request Example
{
  "model": "moonshotai/kimi-k2.5",
  "input": [
    {
      "type": "message",
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Analyze this sensitive business data."
    }
  ],
  "providerOptions": {
    "gateway": {
      "zeroDataRetention": true
    }
  }
}
```

--------------------------------

### ZDR Error Response

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/ai-gateway/security-and-compliance/zdr

This error is returned when no providers supporting Zero Data Retention are available for the requested model.

```json
{
  "error": "No ZDR (Zero Data Retention) providers available for model: example/model-name. \
            Providers considered: provider-a, provider-b",
  "type": "no_providers_available",
  "statusCode": 400
}
```

--------------------------------

### Enforce Zero Data Retention with TypeScript

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/ai-gateway/security-and-compliance

Enable the zeroDataRetention flag within providerOptions to restrict routing to providers with verified ZDR agreements.

```typescript
const result = await streamText({
  model: 'anthropic/claude-opus-4.8',
  prompt: 'Analyze this sensitive data...',
  providerOptions: {
    gateway: { zeroDataRetention: true },
  },
});
```

--------------------------------

### Specify model using gateway provider instance

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/ai-gateway/models-and-providers

Use the gateway function to specify a model provider instance within the AI SDK.

```typescript
import { generateText } from 'ai';
import { gateway } from '@ai-sdk/gateway';
import { NextRequest } from 'next/server';

export async function GET() {
  const result = await generateText({
    model: gateway('anthropic/claude-opus-4.8'),
    prompt: 'Tell me the history of the San Francisco Mission-style burrito.',
  });
  return Response.json(result);
}
```

--------------------------------

### List available models

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/ai-gateway/sdks-and-apis/rest-api

Retrieve a list of all models available through AI Gateway. This endpoint follows the OpenAI models API format and requires no authentication.

```http
GET /v1/models
```

```typescript
const response = await fetch('https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/v1/models');
const { data: models } = await response.json();

models.forEach((model) => {
  console.log(`${model.id}: ${model.name}`);
});
```

--------------------------------

### POST /v1/chat/completions

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/ai-gateway/security-and-compliance/zdr

Enforce Zero Data Retention for chat completion requests using the OpenAI-compatible endpoint. This ensures the request is only handled by providers that have ZDR agreements with Vercel.

```APIDOC
## POST /v1/chat/completions

### Description
Enforce Zero Data Retention for chat completion requests.

### Method
POST

### Endpoint
/v1/chat/completions

### Parameters
#### Request Body
- **model** (string) - Required - The model to use (e.g., moonshotai/kimi-k2.5).
- **messages** (array) - Required - A list of messages comprising the conversation.
- **providerOptions** (object) - Optional - Configuration for the AI Gateway.
  - **gateway** (object) - Optional
    - **zeroDataRetention** (boolean) - Optional - Set to true to route the request only through providers that have zero data retention agreements with Vercel.

### Request Example
{
  "model": "moonshotai/kimi-k2.5",
  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Analyze this sensitive business data."
    }
  ],
  "providerOptions": {
    "gateway": {
      "zeroDataRetention": true
    }
  }
}

### Response
#### Success Response (200)
- **gateway** (object) - Contains routing metadata.
  - **routing** (object)
    - **planningReasoning** (string) - Indicates which providers were considered and the execution order.

#### Error Response (400)
- **error** (string) - Description of the failure.
- **type** (string) - "no_providers_available"
- **statusCode** (number) - 400
```

--------------------------------

### Enforce ZDR with AI SDK

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/ai-gateway/security-and-compliance/zdr

Set zeroDataRetention to true within the gateway providerOptions to ensure compliant routing.

```typescript
import type { GatewayProviderOptions } from '@ai-sdk/gateway';
import { streamText } from 'ai';

export async function POST(request: Request) {
  const result = streamText({
    model: 'moonshotai/kimi-k2.5',
    prompt: 'Analyze this sensitive business data and provide insights.',
    providerOptions: {
      gateway: {
        zeroDataRetention: true,
      } satisfies GatewayProviderOptions,
    },
  });

  return result.toDataStreamResponse();
}
```

```typescript
import type { GatewayProviderOptions } from '@ai-sdk/gateway';
import { generateText } from 'ai';

export async function POST(request: Request) {
  const { text } = await generateText({
    model: 'moonshotai/kimi-k2.5',
    prompt: 'Analyze this sensitive business data and provide insights.',
    providerOptions: {
      gateway: {
        zeroDataRetention: true,
      } satisfies GatewayProviderOptions,
    },
  });

  return Response.json({ text });
}
```

--------------------------------

### Enforce ZDR with Responses API

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/ai-gateway/security-and-compliance/zdr

Use the zeroDataRetention parameter when making direct requests to the Vercel AI Gateway Responses API.

```typescript
const apiKey = process.env.AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY || process.env.VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN;

const response = await fetch('https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/v1/responses', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: {
    'Content-Type': 'application/json',
    Authorization: `Bearer ${apiKey}`,
  },
  body: JSON.stringify({
    model: 'moonshotai/kimi-k2.5',
    input: [
      {
        type: 'message',
        role: 'user',
        content: 'Analyze this sensitive business data and provide insights.',
      },
    ],
    providerOptions: {
      gateway: {
        zeroDataRetention: true,
      },
    },
  }),
});
```

```python
import os
from openai import OpenAI

client = OpenAI(
    api_key=os.getenv("AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY"),
    base_url="https://ai-gateway.vercel.sh/v1",
)

response = client.responses.create(
    model="moonshotai/kimi-k2.5",
    input=[
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Analyze this sensitive business data and provide insights.",
        }
    ],
    extra_body={
        "providerOptions": {
            "gateway": {"zeroDataRetention": True}
        }
    },
)
```

--------------------------------

### Update model selection in config

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/ai-gateway/coding-agents/openai-codex

Modify the model field in ~/.codex/config.toml to switch between different AI providers available through the gateway.

```toml
model = "anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6"
# Or try other models:
# model = "google/gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview"
# model = "openai/gpt-5.5"
```

--------------------------------

### client.responses.create

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/ai-gateway/security-and-compliance/zdr

Create a response using the OpenAI SDK targeting the Vercel AI Gateway with Zero Data Retention enabled.

```APIDOC
## client.responses.create

### Description
Create a response via the OpenAI SDK with Zero Data Retention enabled using the extra_body parameter.

### Method
SDK Method

### Parameters
#### Request Body
- **model** (string) - Required - The model identifier.
- **input** (array) - Required - List of input objects.
- **extra_body** (object) - Required - Used to pass providerOptions to the gateway.
  - **providerOptions** (object)
    - **gateway** (object)
      - **zeroDataRetention** (boolean) - Set to true to enable Zero Data Retention.

### Request Example
```python
response = client.responses.create(
    model="moonshotai/kimi-k2.5",
    input=[
        {
            "role": "user",
            "content": "Analyze this sensitive business data and provide insights.",
        }
    ],
    extra_body={
        "providerOptions": {
            "gateway": {"zeroDataRetention": True}
        }
    },
)
```
```

--------------------------------

### anthropic.messages.create

Source: https://vercel.com/docs/ai-gateway/security-and-compliance/zdr

Create a message using the Anthropic SDK with Zero Data Retention enabled via the Vercel AI Gateway.

```APIDOC
## anthropic.messages.create

### Description
Create a message using the Anthropic SDK with Zero Data Retention enabled.

### Method
SDK Method

### Parameters
#### Request Body
- **model** (string) - Required - The model identifier (e.g., "anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6").
- **messages** (array) - Required - List of message objects containing role and content.
- **providerOptions** (object) - Optional - Gateway configuration options.
  - **gateway** (object)
    - **zeroDataRetention** (boolean) - Set to true to enable Zero Data Retention.

### Request Example
```typescript
const message = await anthropic.messages.create({
  model: 'anthropic/claude-sonnet-4.6',
  messages: [
    {
      role: 'user',
      content: 'Analyze this sensitive business data and provide insights.',
    },
  ],
  providerOptions: {
    gateway: {
      zeroDataRetention: true,
    },
  },
});
```
```

